---
/**
 * Architecture diagram for the Pachanga Community case study.
 *
 * Hand-authored SVG: no runtime, no external request, and readable text for
 * search engines and agents. The page repeats the same structure as text, so
 * the diagram is never the only place the information lives.
 */
---

<figure class="pd-diagram">
  <div class="pd-scroll">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 900 560"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="pd-title pd-desc"
      preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMin meet"
    >
      <title id="pd-title">Arquitectura de Pachanga Community</title>
      <desc id="pd-desc">
        A la izquierda, el flujo de datos: la app de Expo Router y sus pantallas llaman a
        hooks de dominio, que llaman a casos de uso; los casos de uso dependen de puertos y
        los adaptadores los implementan contra Supabase. A la derecha, las capas de Atomic
        Design: particles, atoms, molecules, organisms, layouts y screens.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker
          id="pd-arrow"
          viewBox="0 0 10 10"
          refX="8"
          refY="5"
          markerWidth="7"
          markerHeight="7"
          orient="auto-start-reverse"
        >
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="pd-arrowhead" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- Flow: app -->
      <g>
        <rect class="pd-box" x="24" y="30" width="560" height="64" rx="8" />
        <text class="pd-title" x="44" y="57">src/app/ · Expo Router</text>
        <text class="pd-sub" x="44" y="78">
          rutas por fichero; cada pantalla vive en src/ui/screens/
        </text>
      </g>

      <line class="pd-line" x1="304" y1="98" x2="304" y2="106" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <!-- Flow: hooks -->
      <g>
        <rect class="pd-box" x="24" y="110" width="560" height="64" rx="8" />
        <text class="pd-title" x="44" y="137">Hooks de dominio</text>
        <text class="pd-sub" x="44" y="158">
          estado derivado; la pantalla no conoce de dónde vienen los datos
        </text>
      </g>

      <line class="pd-line" x1="304" y1="178" x2="304" y2="186" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <!-- Flow: use cases -->
      <g>
        <rect class="pd-box pd-box--core" x="24" y="190" width="560" height="64" rx="8" />
        <text class="pd-title" x="44" y="217">Casos de uso · domain/**/use-cases</text>
        <text class="pd-sub" x="44" y="238">
          una regla por caso, con sus pruebas; TypeScript puro y Zod
        </text>
      </g>

      <line class="pd-line" x1="304" y1="258" x2="304" y2="266" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <!-- Flow: ports -->
      <g>
        <rect class="pd-box" x="24" y="270" width="560" height="64" rx="8" />
        <text class="pd-title" x="44" y="297">Puertos · I*Port</text>
        <text class="pd-sub" x="44" y="318">
          el contrato que el dominio necesita, sin saber quién lo cumple
        </text>
      </g>

      <!-- Domain boundary -->
      <line class="pd-boundary" x1="24" y1="352" x2="584" y2="352" />
      <text class="pd-boundary-label" x="24" y="372">frontera del dominio</text>

      <!-- Adapters implement ports: arrow climbs back into the domain -->
      <line class="pd-line" x1="304" y1="376" x2="304" y2="340" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <!-- Flow: adapters -->
      <g>
        <rect class="pd-box" x="24" y="380" width="560" height="64" rx="8" />
        <text class="pd-title" x="44" y="407">Adaptadores · src/adapter</text>
        <text class="pd-sub" x="44" y="428">
          Supabase · in-memory · MMKV · TanStack Query · navegación · notificaciones
        </text>
      </g>

      <line class="pd-line" x1="304" y1="448" x2="304" y2="456" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <!-- Flow: infrastructure -->
      <g>
        <rect class="pd-box pd-box--soft" x="24" y="460" width="560" height="64" rx="8" />
        <text class="pd-title" x="44" y="487">Supabase · red</text>
        <text class="pd-sub" x="44" y="508">
          PostgreSQL, autenticación y sincronización con el dispositivo
        </text>
      </g>

      <!-- Atomic Design -->
      <text class="pd-panel" x="612" y="30">UI · Atomic Design</text>

      <g>
        <rect class="pd-pill" x="612" y="44" width="268" height="40" rx="20" />
        <text class="pd-pill-text" x="746" y="69">particles</text>
      </g>
      <line class="pd-line" x1="746" y1="86" x2="746" y2="94" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <g>
        <rect class="pd-pill" x="612" y="98" width="268" height="40" rx="20" />
        <text class="pd-pill-text" x="746" y="123">atoms</text>
      </g>
      <line class="pd-line" x1="746" y1="140" x2="746" y2="148" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <g>
        <rect class="pd-pill" x="612" y="152" width="268" height="40" rx="20" />
        <text class="pd-pill-text" x="746" y="177">molecules</text>
      </g>
      <line class="pd-line" x1="746" y1="194" x2="746" y2="202" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <g>
        <rect class="pd-pill" x="612" y="206" width="268" height="40" rx="20" />
        <text class="pd-pill-text" x="746" y="231">organisms</text>
      </g>
      <line class="pd-line" x1="746" y1="248" x2="746" y2="256" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <g>
        <rect class="pd-pill" x="612" y="260" width="268" height="40" rx="20" />
        <text class="pd-pill-text" x="746" y="285">layouts</text>
      </g>
      <line class="pd-line" x1="746" y1="302" x2="746" y2="310" marker-end="url(#pd-arrow)" />

      <g>
        <rect class="pd-pill pd-pill--screens" x="612" y="314" width="268" height="40" rx="20" />
        <text class="pd-pill-text pd-pill-text--screens" x="746" y="339">screens</text>
      </g>

      <text class="pd-note" x="612" y="386">
        Cada capa compone la anterior y solo
      </text>
      <text class="pd-note" x="612" y="404">
        habla con la de al lado. Un cambio
      </text>
      <text class="pd-note" x="612" y="422">
        visual no toca la lógica.
      </text>
      <text class="pd-note" x="612" y="458">
        Las pantallas llaman a los hooks
      </text>
      <text class="pd-note" x="612" y="476">
        de dominio: la UI no habla con
      </text>
      <text class="pd-note" x="612" y="494">
        Supabase directamente.
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Flujo real del proyecto: pantalla → hook de dominio → caso de uso → puerto ← adaptador
    → Supabase. El dominio no importa React Native, Expo ni la base de datos; por eso se
    prueba sin infraestructura.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .pd-diagram {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pd-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-paper-warm);
  }

  .pd-diagram svg {
    inline-size: 100%;
    min-inline-size: 44rem;
    block-size: auto;
  }

  .pd-box {
    fill: #fff;
    stroke: #e6e0d6;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .pd-box--soft {
    fill: #fbf9f5;
  }

  .pd-box--core {
    fill: #eef3f7;
    stroke: #cfdde6;
  }

  .pd-pill {
    fill: #fff;
    stroke: #e6e0d6;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .pd-pill--screens {
    fill: #294c60;
    stroke: #294c60;
  }

  .pd-pill-text {
    fill: #4f4b47;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono Variable", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    text-anchor: middle;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .pd-pill-text--screens {
    fill: #f7f4ef;
  }

  .pd-title {
    fill: #1a1a1a;
    font-family: "Plus Jakarta Sans Variable", ui-sans-serif, sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .pd-sub {
    fill: #6f6960;
    font-family: "Plus Jakarta Sans Variable", ui-sans-serif, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .pd-panel {
    fill: #1a1a1a;
    font-family: "Plus Jakarta Sans Variable", ui-sans-serif, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pd-note {
    fill: #6f6960;
    font-family: "Plus Jakarta Sans Variable", ui-sans-serif, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .pd-line {
    stroke: #b8b0a3;
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }

  .pd-arrowhead {
    fill: #b8b0a3;
  }

  .pd-boundary {
    stroke: #c9c1b4;
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-box,
  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-pill {
    fill: var(--color-card);
    stroke: var(--color-border);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-box--soft {
    fill: var(--color-paper-warm);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-box--core {
    fill: var(--color-cobalt-tint);
    stroke: var(--color-cobalt);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-pill--screens {
    fill: var(--color-cobalt);
    stroke: var(--color-cobalt);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-pill-text,
  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-sub,
  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-note {
    fill: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-pill-text--screens {
    fill: var(--color-paper);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-title,
  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-panel {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-line,
  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-boundary {
    stroke: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-arrowhead {
    fill: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }

  [data-theme="dark"] .pd-boundary-label {
    fill: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }

  .pd-boundary-label {
    fill: #9b9388;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono Variable", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .pd-diagram figcaption {
    max-inline-size: 46rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
</style>
